# Packages from omarchy-arm install/omarchy-base.packages (+ packages.extra) left
# out on the ThinkSmart View (7.28 GiB eMMC, 2 GB RAM, 800x1280 touch, no keyboard).
# Format: <package>  <reason>. Sizes are installed sizes with exclusive dependencies.

# x86 emulation and heavy desktop apps
qemu-user-static-binfmt  550 MiB qemu-user-static; x86 emulation, no use here
libreoffice-fresh        466 MiB; office suite, not a tablet job (view PDFs with evince)
obsidian                 432 MiB with its Electron runtime
obs-studio               166 MiB; screen recording/streaming, no hardware encoder path on Adreno 506
kdenlive                 96 MiB; video editor
pinta                    20 MiB + .NET runtime
dotnet-runtime           only needed by pinta
aether                   178 MiB with webkit2gtk-4.1; theme designer
localsend                70 MiB; Flutter app
cliamp                   41 MiB; terminal music player
herdr                    terminal multiplexer (pulls a Zig toolchain on aarch64); not needed
tobi-try                 dev helper
moonlight-qt             game streaming client
gpu-screen-recorder      needs a GPU encoder (VAAPI/NVENC); none on this SoC

# development toolchains and services
clang                    116 MiB
llvm                     87 MiB
docker                   123 MiB daemon on a 2 GB machine
docker-buildx            66 MiB
docker-compose           29 MiB
lazydocker               13 MiB
ufw-docker               only meaningful with docker; firewall.sh skips its rules when absent
mariadb-libs             29 MiB; for ruby/python database gems
postgresql-libs          12 MiB; same
python-poetry-core       Python build backend
tree-sitter-cli          8 MiB; nvim parser builds
lua51                    nvim plugin builds
luarocks                 nvim plugin builds
ruby                     21 MiB; dev environment
mise-bin                 128 MiB; installs the AI CLIs and dev tools. Omarchy gates every mise step on the command existing
omarchy-nvim             56 MiB Omarchy Neovim config (neovim itself stays)

# printing, external displays, PC hardware
cups                     printing
cups-browsed             printing
cups-filters             printing
cups-pdf                 printing
system-config-printer    printing
ddcutil                  DDC/CI for external monitors; the panel is DSI
bolt                     Thunderbolt
asdcontrol               Apple Studio Display
kernel-modules-hook      keeps modules of the running kernel across linux package upgrades; the kernel here is not a package
gvfs-nfs                 network filesystems in Nautilus
gvfs-smb                 network filesystems in Nautilus
gvfs-mtp                 phones over USB; the port is device-mode only

# input and OCR replaced or not useful on a touch tablet
fcitx5                   input method framework; conflicts with the on-screen keyboard (both are input methods). Add back with fcitx5-mozc if a keyboard is attached
fcitx5-gtk               see fcitx5
fcitx5-qt                see fcitx5
tesseract                OCR text extraction from screenshots
tesseract-data-eng       OCR data

# fonts
noto-fonts-cjk           299 MiB; replaced by adobe-source-han-sans-jp-fonts (32 MiB) for Japanese
